  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the following circuit, the battery has an emf of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and an internal resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math>. The power consumption in the entire circuit is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>.</p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/951e50f6-857b-4785-829d-068d6a4705b0.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 257px;\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/951e50f6-857b-4785-829d-068d6a4705b0.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 257px;\"/></p><p>As we can see, two resistances of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> in the middle portion(in both left and right side) are in parallel, so their combined resistance will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math>. Now this resistance along with the topmost &amp; bottommost resistance are in parallel again, so total resistance of the circuit will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
